  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S5070",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5070-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5070\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in\nrelation to a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on\ncertain premises\n\nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis legislation would allow for an exemption to the \"200 Foot Rule\"\nunder the State's Alcoholic Beverage Control Law to allow for Perillo\nHospitality, LLC, doing business as Salumeria Belsito at 1368 Hertel\nAvenue in Buffalo, to apply for an on-premise liquor license from the\nNew York State Liquor Authority.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1- Amends subdivision 7 of § 64 of the Alcoholic Beverage Control\nLaw by adding a new paragraph (e-7).\n\n§ 2- Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSection 64 of New York State's Alcoholic Beverage Control Law states\nthat, \"No retail license for on-premises consumption shall be granted\nfor any premises which shall be (a) on the same street or avenue and\nwithin two hundred feet of a building occupied exclusively as a\nschool, church, synagogue or other place of worship\" often referred to\nas the \"200 Foot Rule\". In very specific instances where the affected\nschool, church, synagogue or other place of worship is not in\nopposition to an application for an on-premise license which would\notherwise not be allowed, the legislature, with written proof of the\naffected entity's acquiescence, allows for an exemption from the \"200\nFoot Rule.\"\n\nThis legislation would allow for an exemption to the \"200 Foot Rule\"\nunder the State's Alcoholic Beverage Control Law to allow for Perillo\nHospitality, LLC, doing business as Salumeria Belsito at 1368 Hertel\nAvenue in Buffalo, to apply for an on-premise liquor license from the\nNew York State Liquor Authority.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
